# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# GLib and GIO are not built with ThreadSanitizer. They free an object when
# an atomic reference count reaches zero, and TSan cannot see that ordering.
# So when the gdbus worker thread drops the last reference to an object that
# the AT-SPI thread used, TSan reports a race in the free. Neither stack has
# a frame in this project. Each entry names one GLib finalizer. Do not add a
# library-wide entry: every GLib thread starts in g_thread_proxy, so it would
# also hide races in project code.
race:g_main_context_unref
race:g_dbus_message_finalize
